From: Stijn Tintel <stijn@linux-ipv6.be>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 13:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: allow drivers to delegate user ports

Some switch fabrics expose ports of another switch through representor
netdevices owned by one control-plane switch.  The DSA user netdevice on
the other switch must stop being a data and configuration endpoint, while
its phylink instance remains running to keep the physical fabric usable.

Add an explicitly RTNL-serialized delegation API.  Delegation is only
allowed for an up, standalone user port without uppers.  Publish the
delegated state before detaching and synchronizing the local netdevice,
then drop both its DSA RX and TX.  Reject new uppers and the DSA
configuration entry points which can otherwise bypass the
detached-netdevice checks.

Closing a delegated user netdevice defers its host address, port and
phylink shutdown.  Undelegation performs that deferred shutdown if
userspace closed the device in the meantime; otherwise it simply
reattaches the running netdevice.  The delegating driver owns hardware
forwarding while the flag is set and must restore local ownership before
undelegating.

Allow the owner to set the physical port's administrative state without
reattaching the original netdevice.  Track that state explicitly so
repeated desired-state operations are idempotent.  On undelegation, restore
the port to the original netdevice's current administrative state.

Signed-off-by: Stijn Tintel <stijn@linux-ipv6.be>
---
 include/net/dsa.h |  19 +++++
 net/dsa/tag.c     |   6 ++
 net/dsa/user.c    | 243 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 3 files changed, 268 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/net/dsa.h b/include/net/dsa.h
--- a/include/net/dsa.h
+++ b/include/net/dsa.h
@@ -296,6 +296,10 @@ struct dsa_port {
 	/* Valid only on user ports */
 	u8			cpu_port_in_lag:1;
 
+	/* Published under RTNL and read locklessly in the data path */
+	bool			delegated;
+	bool			delegated_admin_up;
+
 	u8			setup:1;
 
 	struct device_node	*dn;
@@ -1413,4 +1417,19 @@ netdev_tx_t dsa_enqueue_skb(struct sk_buff *skb, struct net_device *dev);
 void dsa_port_phylink_mac_change(struct dsa_switch *ds, int port, bool up);
+
+/*
+ * Transfer a user port's data and configuration plane to its switch driver.
+ *
+ * The call requires RTNL.  Delegation is not reference counted: the caller
+ * owns the delegated port until it clears the state, and must do so before
+ * unregistering the switch.  The caller must configure its replacement data
+ * path after delegation returns, and restore normal hardware forwarding before
+ * clearing delegation.  DSA initially keeps phylink running; the owner may
+ * change the physical administrative state while delegation remains active.
+ */
+int dsa_port_set_delegated(struct dsa_port *dp, bool delegated,
+			   struct netlink_ext_ack *extack);
+int dsa_port_set_delegated_admin_state(struct dsa_port *dp, bool up);
+
 bool dsa_supports_eee(struct dsa_switch *ds, int port);
 
 #endif
